sample answers for the scenario questions. Looking at the distribution across all three topics, the counts are checking out: HV Safety hits exactly 40%, PPE comes in at 31.4%, and Battery Basics at 28.6%, which all meet the requirements. The answer key is complete at 25 marks across both sections. Now I'm verifying the CoCU references—Q1-Q25 are all tagged properly, and I'm checking through Q26-Q35 to confirm they have their curriculum references as well. Looking at the C01 requirements, I need 11 scenario questions with substantial sample answers to meet the 30% threshold, but there are only 5 currently (Q21-Q25). I could either create 6 new ones or add sample answers to the existing enrichment scenarios Q26-Q35.\n\nFor C02, the situation is more critical—it only has about 18 questions across three sections with no Q-Format bank at all, no CoCU references, and no scenario-based questions. I need to build out a complete 40+ question Q-Format section distributed across the three content areas: BMS theory (14 questions), HV cable systems (14 questions), and OBC (12 questions). I can see the Q-Format structure for C02 needs 40 questions distributed across three topics with scenario questions making up 30% of the total, each with 50+ word sample answers and CoCU references. Now I'm mapping out the implementation steps to add this question bank section to the C02 file.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":9102,"cache_read_input_tokens":36266,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":9102},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"4aad63e8-74bd-4073-a099-f779e2e73025","uuid":"8529d024-b59f-4c3a-add9-43a9b3f5a146"}
